{
 "name": "moose_head_surfacing",
 "description": "A wet moose head and neck rising out of a lake, facing right, mid-chew: dark wet-brown coat, long Roman-nosed face ending in a big bulbous overhanging muzzle (deeper than the mid-face, large slanted nostril, upper lip drooping over a set-back chin), hanging bell under the throat, broad leaf-shaped ears held out sideways, small summer velvet palmate antlers (rounded fuzzy tips), small eye under a heavy brow. Pondweed hangs from the mouth to the water and drapes over the head; drips; ring of white ripples at the waterline. Eye looks straight ahead. Anchor (0,0) = waterline under the neck; x -176..214, y -314..21.",
